        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0214" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2380.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that reports
                    have reached me that there is danger of antiforeign riots in Shansi.</p>
                <p>I have accordingly addressed to the Tsung-li Yemên a communication asking that
                    stringent measures be taken to prevent disorder, of which a copy is
                    inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d165-a1.xml" xpointer="d165-a1"/>
            </div>
